Activity-Relay Directory for Debian/Ubuntu
===========================================

Installation is deliberately separate from activation.

The package installs a dedicated activity-relay-directory system account,
owner-only state directory, /etc/default/activity-relay-directory, an empty
/etc/activity-relay-directory/ operator-config directory, a config.yml example
under /usr/share/doc/activity-relay-directory/examples/, and a hardened systemd
unit. It does not install an active /etc/activity-relay-directory/config.yml.
The service is not enabled or started automatically.

Fresh package defaults bind only to 127.0.0.1:8080 and keep lifecycle,
public listing, automatic soft pruning, positive inactive retention, and
administrator email disabled. Review /etc/default/activity-relay-directory
before manually enabling or starting the unit.

Removal/purge safety
--------------------

Removing the package preserves /var/lib/activity-relay-directory and the
dedicated system account. Purging removes package conffiles in the normal dpkg
manner but intentionally does NOT delete the SQLite database or system account.
This prevents an accidental purge from destroying directory state. After a
verified backup, an administrator who truly wants to destroy the instance must
remove the preserved state and account explicitly.

Downgrade safety
----------------

SQLite schema downgrade is not supported in place. Restore the database backup
taken for the matching older release before starting an older binary.
